1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,980
A young champion named Sohrab grew up

2
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:04,080
seeking his father,

3
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:06,420
the mighty warrior Rostam.

4
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:09,600
War placed them on opposing sides before

5
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:10,949
they could truly meet.

6
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:15,080
Schemes and uncertainty kept the truth concealed.

7
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:18,400
Two unmatched warriors entered combat,

8
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:21,420
each unaware that his opponent was his

9
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:22,073
own blood.

10
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:24,900
Their struggle shook the battlefield.

11
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:28,760
Rostam finally struck a fatal blow,

12
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:32,018
believing he had defeated a dangerous enemy.

13
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:35,920
Only afterward did a token reveal Sohrab’s

14
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:38,980
identity. The victor realized he had killed

15
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,920
the son he had never known.

16
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:43,820
Rostam cried out for help,

17
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:46,520
but the damage could not be reversed.

18
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:49,420
His greatest strength had brought him the

19
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:51,040
worst possible defeat.

20
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:55,340
The Shahnameh preserves a tragedy in which

21
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:59,080
courage cannot compensate for deception and silence.

22
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:02,800
A battlefield victory becomes a lifetime of

23
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:03,260
grief.
